_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-015.mrc:97473027:3517","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.12.20150123.full.mrc:13563593:1135","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_013.bib.mrc:337495247:2684"],"title":"Luminous essence","work_titles":["Gsaṅ ʼgrel phyogs bcuʼi mun sel gyi spyi don ʼod gsal sñiṅ po."],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes index.\r\n\r\nTranslated from Tibetan."},"identifiers":{"goodreads":["6634331"],"librarything":["8429188"]},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"dewey_decimal_class":["294.3/85"],"subjects":["Tripiṭaka. -- Sūtrapiṭaka. -- Tantra. -- Guhyagarbhatantra -- Criticism, interpretation, etc"],"publish_date":"2009","publish_country":"nyu","by_statement":"by Jamgon Mipham ; foreword by His Holiness the Dalai Lama ; translated by the Dharmachakra Translation Committee.","oclc_numbers":["289070790"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL15106454W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"[Book title] is a complete introduction to the world of tantric thought and practice. Composed by the renowned Tibetan master [author], the text provides an overview of the theory and experiential assimilation of a seminal tantric scripture, the Tantra of the Secret Essence (Guhyagarbha Tantra). Embodying the essence of tantric practice, this text has been a central scripture in Tibetan Buddhism for well over a thousand years. [author's] explanation of this text, here translated for the first time, is one of the most celebrated commentaries on the Tantra of the Secret Essence, which today occupies an important place in the tantric curriculum of Tibetan monastic colleges.\"--Book jacket."},"number_of_pages":174,"latest_revision":19,"revision":19,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2009-01-07T18:17:20.098220"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-08-17T17:10:18.578292"}}},"ISBN:9780892541690":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780892541690","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL25005393M/Tan